            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> `MarkedString` sounds like exactly what we need!\n> \n> And yes this may require enhancing `vim.lsp.buf.hover`\n\nUnfortunately, after reading more carefully, `MarkedString` is marked as `@deprecated use MarkupContent instead.`. And the (currently supported and used in `vim.pack`) `MarkupContent` [only supports `plaintext` or `markdown`](https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/specifications/lsp/3.17/specification/#markupContentInnerDefinition). With a more or less direct suggestion to used fenced code blocks: ``If the kind is `markdown` then the value can contain fenced code blocks like in GitHub issues.``\n\nSo I don't think enhancing `vim.lsp.buf.hover` to support deprecated method is the way to go here. For reference: `MarkedString` is already deliberately [converted to markdown](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/08a1228f8243415d199f4a6c3adce8dc1b36b551/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/buf.lua#L168) which [just makes a fenced code block](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/08a1228f8243415d199f4a6c3adce8dc1b36b551/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/util.lua#L606-L608).\n\n---\n\nHere are ways of resolving this that I can think of:\n\n1. Bundle `diff` tree-sitter parser+queries. There is no need autoenable it anywhere, it will work as is with autoenabled tree-sitter in markdown.\n    1.a. Document that to get the diff highlighting, there needs to be `diff` parser+queries available. Resolved neovim/neovim#39006 would help here with queries, but not with parser (as far as I understand the scope).\n3. Hack in-process `vim.pack` LSP server `methods['textDocument/hover']` to execute callback and (somehow) adjust content of the opened window. This won't work universally, since users can define their own `textDocument/hover` handlers that act differently.\n4. Make custom `K` mapping in the confirmation buffer that somehow enforces built-in floating window and (somehow) enforce the filetype. This makes users with custom `vim.lsp.buf.hover` mappings not happy and diminishes the point of going the in-process LSP route.\n5. Use completely custom logic for showing the floating window with the diff. Not good because of more duplicated code, in general not the best look for the in-process LSP server, etc.\n\nSo I think that the 1. is the best course of action here. Short-term: add something like ``For highlighting the output install |treesitter| `diff` parser and `highlight.scm` |treesitter-query|``. Long-term: bundle `diff` parser and its queries *or* have an \"officially recommended\" way to install them (with `vim.pack.add`).",
