            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I don't remember either. It currently only supports the git-style unified diff format, which makes it unsuitable for a general replacement for the legacy syntax file (which supports multiple formats). But that is not an issue for this specific use case (assuming people don't change the default).\n\nI was also cautious about this being a third-party parser we have no control over, but in the meantime I got the Helix dev to kindly donate the repo (but we still share custody so we shouldn't go ham with it).",
